Comments:
Evaluated by Caleb Marshall 2025
1) Resonances adopted from Rogers 1971, Rogers 1972, Rogers 1973, Rogers 1976, Smotrich 1961, Dixon and Story 1972b, Dixon and Story 1977, Aitken 1969a, Aitken 1969b, Underwood 1974, Symons 1978, Wilmes 2002, Di Leva  2017, Fang 2024, Volya 2022.
2) All resonances normalized to the strength of the 1324 keV resonance, which was taken to be the weighted average of Dixon and Story 1971a, Aitken 1969, Wilmes 2002, Di Leva 2017, Fang 2024, 
3) Direct capture based on spectroscopic factors of Mao 1996 (with radius 1.4 fm).
4) Factor of 3 uncertainty adopted for partial widths derived from de Oliveira 1996 and Fortune 2010 due in part to factor of 3 disagreement with Mao and higher lying resonances that have been directly observed with Fortune 2003, Fortune 2010.
5) Excitation energies of 1324 and 1487 keV resonances deduced from gamma energies reported in Fang 2024 using the method discribed in Helmer 1978. All other values taken from Tilly 1995.